  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Calinerie, on avenue de Provence in Fréjus, is the oldest grooming salon in Fréjus and Saint-Raphaël according to its official website: founded in 1983, taken over by Thierry in 1996 and renovated in 2016 for the animals' comfort. Each dog is groomed one-on-one, entirely by Thierry himself, and the work is done in full view of the public — a deliberate transparency.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The salon is open Monday to Friday, from 9am to 12:30pm then 2 to 5pm. Free parking on site. Appointments are made by phone (04 94 51 05 54) or through the online calendar on the website.</p>
      <p>The package includes the cut, a hot-water wash with dog shampoo, drying, nail clipping and removal of hair inside the ears. Prices published by the salon:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Clipping package (3 to 5 mm): €46 for a dog under 5 kg, €56 from 5 to 15 kg, €66 from 15 to 20 kg;</li>
        <li>Cut package (scissors and clippers): €53, €64 and €79 for the same weight bands;</li>
        <li>dogs over 20 kg: by quote.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Worth checking:</strong> the online booking page says the salon only takes small and medium dogs of 20 kg maximum, while the price page provides a quote above 20 kg. For a large dog, call before you come.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book before arriving in Fréjus if you'll be there in summer.</div>
    </div>

